+      # unless impossible): apt on ubuntu-26.04 "resolute" (the actual
+      # matrix OS, not 24.04) ships mkvtoolnix 97.0-1build1; choco and
+      # brew both currently track 100.0(.0) - majors diverge, so pin
+      # where the manager allows an install-time version. apt and choco
+      # do; both are pinned below. Homebrew's core tap keeps no versioned
+      # mkvtoolnix formula and no install-time version selector (`brew
+      # pin` only locks an already-installed version against a later
+      # `brew upgrade`), so brew floats on latest stable - the one
+      # manager where pinning is not idiomatically possible. The apt pin
+      # is an exact build (`-1build1`); an archive rebuild can supersede
+      # that string and will need a bump, same maintenance shape as the
+      # SHA-pin policy above.
+      - name: Install mkvtoolnix (gated integration tests, Linux)
