+      # Task 2 (#14): assert the gated tests actually exercised mkvmerge
+      # instead of silently self-skipping, now that mkvtoolnix is
+      # installed on every leg. --nocapture is required: cargo test
+      # captures stdout/stderr of PASSING tests by default, so the
+      # self-skip eprintln would be invisible without it. --test-threads=1
+      # avoids --nocapture output from concurrent test threads interleaving
+      # and corrupting the marker line. A genuinely missing mkvmerge
+      # (install regression) trips the count above zero and fails the
+      # step - "otherwise silent skipping is traded for silent skipping"
+      # (walkthrough #14).
+      - name: Assert no gated tests silently skip (mkvmerge missing)
+        shell: bash
+        run: |
+          cargo test --workspace -- --nocapture --test-threads=1 2>&1 | tee gated-test-output.log
+          count="$(grep -c 'mkvmerge not found; skipping' gated-test-output.log || true)"
+          echo "Skip-marker occurrences: $count"
+          if [ "$count" -ne 0 ]; then
+            echo "::error::$count gated integration test(s) silently skipped (mkvmerge not found on PATH) - expected 0 now that mkvtoolnix is installed on every leg."
+            exit 1
+          fi
